@startuml "Flyweight - Tile Map (Homework) - Class Diagram"
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members
title Flyweight — homework 1: 250,000 squares, five kinds of ground


class Tile <<ConcreteFlyweight>> {
  - terrain : String
  - movementCost : int
  - sprite : byte[]
  + render(row, column)
}

class TileFactory <<FlyweightFactory>> {
  - tiles : Map<String, Tile>
  + get(terrain, cost) : Tile
}

class SpriteLoader {
  + load(terrain) : byte[]
  + loadCount() : int
}

class GameMap {
  - squares : Tile[][]
  + rowMovementCost(row) : int
}

GameMap o--> Tile : "one reference per square"
TileFactory ..> Tile
TileFactory --> SpriteLoader

note right of GameMap
  A <b>Tile[][]</b> holds references, so the
  map costs one pointer per square
  whatever the artwork weighs.

  250,000 squares -> <b>5</b> objects,
  <b>5</b> sprite loads.
end note

@enduml
